            <ArticleTitle>Pre-clinical Training for New Notes Procedures: From Ex-vivo Models to Virtual Reality Simulators.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>401-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.giec.2015.12.007</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1052-5157(15)00136-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Natural orifice transluminal endoscopic surgery (NOTES) is a newer field of endoscopic surgery that allows for scarless treatment of pathologic entities, using novel transluminal approaches. There has been a shift of focus from a clinical and research standpoint from the development and dissemination of &quot;first-generation&quot; NOTES procedures to &quot;new NOTES&quot; procedures that traverse the mucosa of luminal structures, yet do not stray far into the peritoneal cavity. It has been a challenge to find appropriate and effective ways to train gastroenterologists and surgeons in these novel approaches. We review the importance of simulation in training and discuss available simulation options.</AbstractText>
